;; Samus's mini game, Zebes Escape: the cavern under 4-2 as it self-destructs. Three screens wide
;; and three high (`camera: free`, `height: 45`: the camera follows up and down the shafts).
;; stage.ts loads it with ?raw, so it is not in the level library, the dev level select or the
;; campaign.
;;
;; The route: the Chozo chamber (bottom left) -> the corridor (a pit, a morph-ball tunnel with a
;; bomb block) -> shaft 1 up (bottom right) -> the middle corridor left (a bomb wall) -> shaft 2 up
;; (left) -> the top corridor right (a second morph-ball tunnel) -> down into the hangar -> the ship.
;; Platforms (B) step up three rows at a time, each beside the last and never right above a
;; take-off spot: every climb is a jump up beside a ledge and a drift onto it (no wall jump).
;; The creatures, the statue, the alarm lights and the ship are the mini game's own entity types
;; (World's extraEntities, stage.ts).
id: zebes-escape
name: ZEBES ESCAPE
world: 4
stage: 2
theme: cavern
music: zebes-escape
time: 400
start: 3,42
startMode: stand
camera: free
height: 45

